<article class="env-lemma" id="024G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/024G">Lemma <span data-tag="024G">85.31.1</span>.</a> Let $X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Suppose $Y \to (X/S)_\bullet $ is a cartesian morphism of simplicial schemes. For $y \in Y_0$ a point define </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  T_ y = \{ y' \in Y_0 \mid \exists \  y_1 \in Y_1: d^1_1(y_1) = y, d^1_0(y_1) = y'\}   \]
</div>
  <p> as a subset of $Y_0$. Then $y \in T_ y$ and $T_ y \cap T_{y'} \not= \emptyset \Rightarrow T_ y = T_{y'}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Lemma <a href="/tag/024E" data-tag="024E">85.30.1</a> and Groupoids, Lemma <a href="/tag/022Q" data-tag="022Q">39.3.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>